<title>CHINA: CIBC SETS CHEUNG KONG INFRA WARRANTS.</title>
<headline>CIBC SETS CHEUNG KONG INFRA WARRANTS.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London branch of the Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce said on Tuesday it had launched 100 million American-style call warrants on shares of Cheung Kong Infrastructure Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one share.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE     HK$31.453	PREMIUM	 34 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	HK$0.52	  GEARING	 5.26x</p>
<p> LAUNCH DATE	12.AUG.97	MIN EXER LOT  10,000</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	 12.AUG.98	LISTING	 HONG KONG</p>
<p> REFERENCE SPOT   HK$27.35</p>
<p> NOTE		 PHYSICAL OR CASH SETTLEMENT AT ISSUER'S</p>
<p>			DISCRETION</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
